    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d69">

                <pb facs="0183" n="79" xml:id="pg79"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Mizner</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-19"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 19,
                        1890</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 155.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 126 of the 28th
                    ultimo, acknowledging the receipt on the 23d ultimo, through Mr. Ryan, of the
                    Department’s telegram of the 19th of the same month, relating to the seizure by
                    the Guatemalan Government of the arms on board the steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Colima.</hi></p>
                <p>Consideration of this subject is necessarily deferred until your further
                    dispatches shall place the whole case before the Department and the action of
                    the Gutemalan Government upon your demands in respect to this unjustifiable
                    seizure shall be known.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton.</hi><lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
